course: dictionary
lesson: 3613
title: Fille: girl or daughter
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Fille» is a French word, so you will not find it in English. It means girl, and it can also mean daughter. «Une petite fille» means a little girl, and «ma fille» means my daughter. Read the words around it to work out which meaning fits.
explain: «Fille» sounds like "feey", with a soft y at the end. It is a feminine noun, so it goes with «une» or «la». You say «une fille» for a girl, and «la fille» for the girl or the daughter.
explain: Do not mix it up with English words that look similar. «Fill» means to make full, and «file» is a folder or a tool. «Je suis une fille» means I am a girl, and it always takes «une», the girl word, not «un».
fact: «Fille» means girl or daughter in French.
fact: «Une fille» means a girl, and «un garçon» means a boy.
fact: «Ma fille» means my daughter.
fact: «Jeune fille» means young lady, and grown-ups use it too.
fact: An only daughter is «fille unique», and «enfant unique» works for any child.
exercise: «Je suis une fille.» What does «fille» mean here? | A town | A boy | A thousand | *A girl
exercise: «Ma fille» is French. What does it mean? | *my daughter | my mother | my file | my town
exercise: Which article goes with «fille»? | le | *une | les | un
test: Which word is the boy form, as in «un fils» and «une fille»? | fille | cousine | tante | *fils
test: Which English word should you not mix up with «fille»? | child | girl | daughter | *file
exam: Which phrase means young lady? | une petite fille | *jeune fille | enfant unique | fille unique
